{"profile":{"name":"Jennifer McKelvie","ward":"Ward 25, Scarborough—Rouge Park","bio":"Jennifer McKelvie represented Ward 25, Scarborough-Rouge Park on Toronto City Council from 2018 until she resigned on May 9, 2025, having been re-elected in 2022 with 72.3% of the vote. A professional geoscientist with a PhD in geology from the University of Toronto, she previously managed research partnerships at the Nuclear Waste Management Organization and the Canadian Institute for Advanced Research. She served as Deputy Mayor of Toronto (2022-2023) and as chair of the Infrastructure and Environment Committee; she left council after being elected as the Liberal Member of Parliament for Ajax in the April 28, 2025 federal election.","committees":["Infrastructure and Environment Committee (Chair)","Executive Committee","Scarborough Community Council","Toronto Transit Commission","Budget Committee","Board of Directors of Toronto Hydro","Toronto Zoo Board of Management (Chair)"],"contact":{"email":"councillor_mckelvie@toronto.ca","phone":"416-338-3771"},"promises":[{"text":"Advance the Eglinton East LRT as a service-first priority for Scarborough.","source":"https://cliffcrestscarboroughvillagesw.ca/data/documents/2025-Rouge-Ward-25-By-election-Flashcard-FINAL.pdf"},{"text":"Tackle basement flooding affecting Scarborough homes.","source":"https://cliffcrestscarboroughvillagesw.ca/data/documents/2025-Rouge-Ward-25-By-election-Flashcard-FINAL.pdf"},{"text":"Protect ravines and manage growth responsibly.","source":"https://cliffcrestscarboroughvillagesw.ca/data/documents/2025-Rouge-Ward-25-By-election-Flashcard-FINAL.pdf"}]},"lobbying":{"total":726,"term":312,"first":"2018-12-10","last":"2025-05-06","lobbyists":179,"clients":143,"subjects":311,"methods":{"Meetings":254,"Emails":359,"Phone calls":71,"Written":20,"Other or unreported":22},"top":[{"label":"Economic Development","count":175},{"label":"By-law / Regulation","count":124},{"label":"Transportation","count":100},{"label":"Envir